            <div xml:id="d860">

                <pb facs="0911" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123R27/14: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul in Chargé at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-16T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 16,
                                1920—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>If Spiker has reached Shanghai in matter of Chang Ching-yao, in struct him to
                    return to Peking and leave investigation entirely in <pb facs="0912" n="814"
                        xml:id="pg814"/> hands of Consulate. If Chang is in Shanghai report fact to
                    Legation with request that Legation ask Chinese Government to institute
                    proceedings for his arrest and trial.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
